        // grantRole will succeed only if this contract has admin role for `role` — constructor set admin of TIMELOCK_ADMIN_ROLE to itself and others to TIMELOCK_ADMIN_ROLE
        // To ensure grantRole works, set role's admin to TIMELOCK_ADMIN_ROLE by calling setRoleAdmin via schedule/execute is impossible here; however in reference constructor,
        // _setRoleAdmin(PROPOSER_ROLE, TIMELOCK_ADMIN_ROLE); etc. For arbitrary role derived here, its admin defaults to bytes32(0) which is DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE,
        // and this contract has DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE (TIMELOCK_ADMIN_ROLE was setup for address(this) and address(this) has DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE? In reference C, DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE is 0x00 and nobody was setup for that explicitly except TIMELOCK_ADMIN_ROLE and address(this) got TIMELOCK_ADMIN_ROLE but not DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE.
        // To ensure we can grant the fuzzed role, we'll instead grant via internal-visible public API _setupRole is internal. But we cannot call internal. However we can test a role that already exists: use one of the defined roles like PROPOSER_ROLE.

    }
}

